build	refused	`BagIterator` is a `borrows struct` and may not be produced from a TEMPORARY receiver: a borrowing struct holds a LENT PLACE, so its values live only inside their window — the extent is the `for` statement, which is what makes the borrow trackable without a lifetime. Bind the collection first (`let c = make()` then `for x in c.iter()`): a temporary has no persistent storage for the window to point into
