log	"error: the inferred return type of a closure may not name a borrowing struct: `BagIterator` is a `borrows struct`, and a borrowing struct holds a LENT PLACE, so its values live only inside their window — the extent is the `for` statement, which is what makes the borrow trackable without a lifetime. A type argument, an existential, a field, a parameter and a plain return each outlive the window, so none of them can name one — which is what makes a generic identity wrapper unwritable rather than caught"
log	"  --> examples/errors/borrowing_struct_value_positions.saw:125:16"
log	"      |"
log	" 125 |     let f = { b.iter() }                    // ROW 8: a closure's returned value"
log	"      |                ^"
log	"   hint: the one declaration that may name it is the `borrows` producer that RETURNS it (`func iter(&self) borrows -> VectorIterator<T>`) and the type's own extension methods"
